# Fast Flights Project Structure

This is a Google Flights scraper library built with Python. The main entry points are:

## Core Package Structure
- [fast_flights/](mdc:fast_flights/) - Main package directory
  - [__init__.py](mdc:fast_flights/__init__.py) - Main exports and public API
  - [querying.py](mdc:fast_flights/querying.py) - Query building and data structures
  - [fetcher.py](mdc:fast_flights/fetcher.py) - HTTP fetching logic
  - [parser.py](mdc:fast_flights/parser.py) - HTML/JSON parsing logic
  - [model.py](mdc:fast_flights/model.py) - Data models and dataclasses
  - [types.py](mdc:fast_flights/types.py) - Type definitions and enums
  - [pb/](mdc:fast_flights/pb/) - Protocol Buffer definitions and generated code
  - [integrations/](mdc:fast_flights/integrations/) - Integration adapters (BrightData, etc.)

## Legacy Code
- [legacy/](mdc:legacy/) - Contains the old implementation for reference
- [legacy/fast_flights/](mdc:legacy/fast_flights/) - Legacy package structure

## Key Files
- [main.py](mdc:main.py) - Example usage with old API
- [test.py](mdc:test.py) - Example usage with new API
- [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml) - Project configuration and dependencies
- [README.md](mdc:README.md) - Comprehensive documentation and API examples

## Development Files
- [docs/](mdc:docs/) - Documentation files
- [examples/](mdc:examples/) - Usage examples
- [scripts/](mdc:scripts/) - Utility scripts
- [enums/](mdc:enums/) - Generated airport enums

The project uses Protocol Buffers for Google Flights API communication and supports multiple integration backends.